<p>For the first time after China enters the WTO, this exhibition mainly
covers the latest technology, new product and solution in the field of
e-government infrastructure, e-government application and e-government
information security. Meanwhile, the e-Government China 2002 Forum will
be organized to discuss the prospect, strategy and application on China
e-government development, targeting government officials, consulting expe=
rts
and corporate delegates.
<p>The exhibition aims to provide an open and interactive platform for
both e-government users and builders through products demonstration, spec=
ial
forums and promotional activities. With the strong supports of most China
central ministries and departments, the exhibition invites various delega=
tions
and individuals from ministries, provinces, cities and industries. Being
the top-level IT exhibition in China, e-Government China Expo will be hel=
d
annually focusing on the promotion of e-government application in China.
<p><b>The exhibition area</b> is up to 15000sqm=A1Awhich invites over 100=
,000
delegates from China and abroad. Exhibitors include IT manufacturers, sof=
tware
vendors, solution providers, service providers, etc. The exhibition is
divided into 3 sections as follow:
